        "id": "def-ip-composite-double-regularization",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Composite double regularization",
        "statement": "Let $X,Y,Z$ be real or complex Hilbert spaces over one scalar field, let $F:X\\to Y$ and $G:Y\\to Z$ be compact linear maps, and set $A:=G\\circ F:X\\to Z$. For spectral regularization families $R^G_\\alpha:Z\\to Y$ for $G^\\dagger$ and $R^F_\\gamma:Y\\to X$ for $F^\\dagger$, and a parameter rule $(\\alpha,\\gamma):(0,\\infty)\\times Z\\to(0,\\infty)^2$, define $T_\\delta(z^\\delta):=R^F_{\\gamma(\\delta,z^\\delta)}(R^G_{\\alpha(\\delta,z^\\delta)}z^\\delta)$ for $z^\\delta\\in Z$. The order is fixed by the factorization: first regularize $G$, then $F$; no general identity $A^\\dagger=F^\\dagger G^\\dagger$ is part of this definition.",
        "deps": [
          "def-ip-compact-linear-inverse-model",
          "def-compact-spectral-filter-and-qualification"
        ],
