      {
        "id": "thm-ip-double-discrepancy-conditional-convergence",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Conditional convergence of double-discrepancy composite inversion",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X,Y,Z$ be real or complex Hilbert spaces over one scalar field. Let compact linear maps $F:X\\to Y$ and $G:Y\\to Z$ have a common singular system indexed by a finite or countable set $J$: $(x_j)_{j\\in J}$, $(y_j)_{j\\in J}$, and $(z_j)_{j\\in J}$ are orthonormal bases of $\\overline{R(F^*)}$, $\\overline{R(F)}=\\overline{R(G^*)}$, and $\\overline{R(G)}$, and $Fx_j=\\lambda_jy_j$, $F^*y_j=\\lambda_jx_j$, $Gy_j=\\mu_jz_j$, and $G^*z_j=\\mu_jy_j$ with $0<\\lambda_j,\\mu_j\\le1$. Put $A:=G\\circ F$. Let $\\nu_0>2$, $1<\\nu\\le\\nu_0-1$, $\\rho>0$, $x^\\dagger=|A|^\\nu w$ with $\\|w\\|_X\\le\\rho$, and $z:=Ax^\\dagger\\ne0$; set $y^\\dagger:=Fx^\\dagger$. The common system gives the compatible minimum-norm factorization on this exact datum: $A^\\dagger z=F^\\dagger G^\\dagger z=x^\\dagger$ and $G^\\dagger z=Fx^\\dagger=y^\\dagger$. For $H=F,G$, let $R^H_\\eta=f^H_\\eta(H^*H)H^*$ and $p^H_\\eta(t):=1-tf^H_\\eta(t)$. Assume finite constants $C_H,S_H,K_H>0$ satisfy $\\|HR^H_\\eta\\|\\le C_H$, $\\|I-HR^H_\\eta\\|\\le S_H$, and $\\|R^H_\\eta\\|\\le K_H\\eta^{-1/2}$ for every $\\eta>0$; and, for each $0<s\\le\\nu_0$, $ up_{j\\in J}s_{H,j}^{s}|p^H_\\eta(s_{H,j}^2)|\\le D_H(s)\\eta^{s/2}$ for finite $D_H(s)$, where $s_{F,j}=\\lambda_j$ and $s_{G,j}=\\mu_j$. Fix $\\tau_G>S_G$ and $\\tau_F>S_FC_G$. Let $\\alpha_k,\\gamma_\\ell>0$ be decreasing sequences with successive ratios in $[\\theta,1)$ for one fixed $0<\\theta<1$. For noisy data $z^\\delta$ with $\\|z^\\delta-z\\|_Z\\le\\delta$, choose first indices $k,\\ell$ (when they exist) such that $\\|GR^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-z^\\delta\\|_Z\\le\\tau_G\\delta<\\|GR^G_{\\alpha_i}z^\\delta-z^\\delta\\|_Z$ for every $i<k$, and $\\|AR^F_{\\gamma_\\ell}R^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-GR^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta\\|_Z\\le\\tau_F\\delta<\\|AR^F_{\\gamma_i}R^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-GR^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta\\|_Z$ for every $i<\\ell$. For any sequence $\\delta\\downarrow0$ for which both selected indices exist for all sufficiently small $\\delta$, there are constants $C_1,C_2$ independent of $\\delta$ and $\\rho$ such that, for all sufficiently small $\\delta$, $\\|x^\\dagger-R^F_{\\gamma_\\ell}R^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta\\|_X\\le C_1\\rho^{1/(\\nu+1)}\\delta^{\\nu/(\\nu+1)}+C_2\\rho^{2/(\\nu+1)}\\delta^{(\\nu-1)/(\\nu+1)}.$ In particular, for fixed $\\rho$ this two-stage reconstruction converges to $x^\\dagger$. The statement is conditional on existence of both stopping indices and makes no claim that $(G\\circ F)^\\dagger=F^\\dagger G^\\dagger$ for arbitrary factorizations.",
