      {
        "id": "op-ip-optimal-composite-discrepancy-rate",
        "kind": "open-problem",
        "title": "Optimal rate for composite double discrepancy",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $X,Y,Z$ be real or complex Hilbert spaces over one scalar field. Let compact linear maps $F:X\\to Y$ and $G:Y\\to Z$ have a common singular system indexed by a finite or countable set $J$: $(x_j)_{j\\in J}$, $(y_j)_{j\\in J}$, and $(z_j)_{j\\in J}$ are orthonormal bases of $\\overline{R(F^*)}$, $\\overline{R(F)}=\\overline{R(G^*)}$, and $\\overline{R(G)}$, and $Fx_j=\\lambda_jy_j$, $F^*y_j=\\lambda_jx_j$, $Gy_j=\\mu_jz_j$, and $G^*z_j=\\mu_jy_j$ with $0<\\lambda_j,\\mu_j\\le1$. Put $A:=G\\circ F$. Let $\\nu_0>2$, $1<\\nu\\le\\nu_0-1$, $\\rho>0$, $w\\in X$ with $\\|w\\|_X\\le\\rho$, $x^\\dagger:=|A|^\\nu w$ where $|A|=(A^*A)^{1/2}$, and $z:=Ax^\\dagger\\ne0$. The common system makes $x^\\dagger$ and $Fx^\\dagger$ the minimum-norm solutions at their respective stages. For $H=F,G$, let $R^H_\\eta:=f^H_\\eta(H^*H)H^*$ and $p^H_\\eta(t):=1-tf^H_\\eta(t)$. Assume finite constants $C_H,S_H,K_H>0$ satisfy $\\|HR^H_\\eta\\|\\le C_H$, $\\|I-HR^H_\\eta\\|\\le S_H$, and $\\|R^H_\\eta\\|\\le K_H\\eta^{-1/2}$ for every $\\eta>0$; and, for every $0<s\\le\\nu_0$, assume a finite constant $D_H(s)$ satisfies $ up_{j\\in J}s_{H,j}^{s}|p^H_\\eta(s_{H,j}^2)|\\le D_H(s)\\eta^{s/2}$ for every $\\eta>0$, where $s_{F,j}=\\lambda_j$ and $s_{G,j}=\\mu_j$. Fix $\\tau_G>S_G$ and $\\tau_F>S_FC_G$. Let $(\\alpha_k)_{k\\ge1}$ and $(\\gamma_\\ell)_{\\ell\\ge1}$ be decreasing positive sequences with successive ratios in $[\\theta,1)$ for one fixed $0<\\theta<1$. For noisy data $z^\\delta$ with $\\|z^\\delta-z\\|_Z\\le\\delta$, choose the first indices $k,\\ell$, when they exist, such that $\\|GR^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-z^\\delta\\|_Z\\le\\tau_G\\delta<\\|GR^G_{\\alpha_i}z^\\delta-z^\\delta\\|_Z$ for every $i<k$, and $\\|AR^F_{\\gamma_\\ell}R^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-GR^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta\\|_Z\\le\\tau_F\\delta<\\|AR^F_{\\gamma_i}R^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-GR^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta\\|_Z$ for every $i<\\ell$. For fixed factors, filters, parameter sequences and radius $\\rho$, define $E_\\delta$ as the supremum of $\\|R^F_{\\gamma_\\ell}R^G_{\\alpha_k}z^\\delta-x^\\dagger\\|_X$ over all $w$ and all $z^\\delta$ satisfying these source, noise, nonzero-data, and stopping-index conditions. Determine the sharp asymptotic order of $E_\\delta$ as $\\delta\\downarrow0$ whenever this admissible set is nonempty. In particular, is the exponent $(\\nu-1)/(\\nu+1)$ in the upper bound $C_1\\rho^{1/(\\nu+1)}\\delta^{\\nu/(\\nu+1)}+C_2\\rho^{2/(\\nu+1)}\\delta^{(\\nu-1)/(\\nu+1)}$ optimal for fixed $\\rho$, or can it be improved uniformly over this composite class?",
